Not really an answer to your question, but why would {zu'e mi viska ko'a} 
expand into {mi zuxte lo nu mi viska ko'a}? Who said that {mi} suddenly 
should occupy viska1? Couldn't a statement of the sort {zu'e mi do viska 
mi} = "By my volition, you saw me"? I.e. the {zo'e} in x1 shouldn't 
necessarely have the same referent as the {zo'e} in the {zu'e} tag... 
should it?

